      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "YES PLEASE VRCHAT let imposters work for the client-user avatar!\n\nRestricting this feature to only the avatars of *others* is sorely confusing and gives the impression that the client is bugged.\n\nThere may be times when a player uses a client different from their norm due to circumstance or for beta testing. Allowing them to *see* their own avatar, even if it's just the imposter, is considerably better than loading a robot, *especially* if the client user is able to see the same imposter on another user.\n\nThe current limitation really induces a \"WTF? Why isn't it working\" UX at the moment.\n\nAnd, to hit it home: imagine you're a PC player who happened to go outside the home. You decide to fire up VRCHAT on your phone, and encounter someone with a cool AF avatar, in imposter form. You want to clone it, to bookmark it and check it out later, but you can't! **Why?** You can see it! It's right there! Why can *they* wear it on mobile, but *you* can't?!\n\nSuffice to say, this feels like a huge oversight of user expectations.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
