  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-12-06T17:49:35.077Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I’ve always been under the impression that after generating an impostor for an avatar, such as iOS, I would then be able to log into the iOS version of the game and see the impostor for that avatar locally.\n\nThis never seems to be the case. Any avatars I’ve generated impostors for still show up as a “caution bot” when worn and I can’t see my own avatar. Why make impostors remote-only? They should be visible to all users, including the wearer.\n\nThis should work the same across all platforms. If a Quest player uses an avatar that isn’t actively uploaded to Android but has an Impostor, they should be able to see that impostor on their own body locally too.",
